# Master cases

Which verb the Master may press at which status, read while `master.mode` is not `off`. Copy this file to
`master-cases.md` to edit a case; a case your copy lacks is read from here. A press at a status no case names is not
made: it is written to `misses.jsonl` beside `state.json` instead, and the task stops for you. `master.mine` and
`humanPaths` still keep a press yours where a case allows it.

Each case: `move:` a verb the Master presses · `at:` the task's statuses, `any` or `any but <statuses>` ·
`by: master` · one line saying what the case is. A step the Master sends the session is a case `by: master` in
`session-cases.md`.

## ship

move: ship
at: REVIEW_PENDING
by: master
The Master read the hand-back, it holds, and the Master ships it.

## reply

move: reply
at: REVIEW_PENDING
by: master
On the Master's ship the session posts its drafted replies to the reviewers.

## deploy

move: deploy
at: REVIEWED, APPROVED
by: master
The request is green with every thread closed, and the Master deploys it once.

## deploy-finish

move: deploy
at: DEPLOY_CONFLICT
by: master
The session staged a deploy conflict resolved in full, and the Master finishes the deploy you pressed.

## approve-plan

move: approve-plan
at: PLAN_PENDING
by: master
The Master read the plan, it holds, and the Master approves it.

## add-repo

move: add-repo
at: any but DONE
by: master
The session asked for a repository its task lacks, and the Master adds it.
